 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Furrows vs. Contact:** Blobs should not stick together; real cloud blobs have furrows. The offset parameter $\epsilon$ in $m_i(P)$ must be set $>0$ (e.g., $0.5$) to repulse surfaces more than for simple contact [S1].
-*   **Level 0 Initialization:** Level 0 has no previous surface $S_{-1}$. It must be created procedurally or manually. Procedural generation on a horizontal plane may result in flat bases; manual placement allows for complex features like turrets [S1].
